":"https://dedigital.dde.pr/pluginfile.php/145102/mod_resource/content/6/Est%C3%A1ndares%20y%20Expectativas%20Programa%20de%20Ingl%C3%A9s.pdf"}],[0,"4.W.5","","standard","Writing",{"withheld":1,"src":"https://dedigital.dde.pr/pluginfile.php/145102/mod_resource/content/6/Est%C3%A1ndares%20y%20Expectativas%20Programa%20de%20Ingl%C3%A9s.pdf"}],[0,"4.W.5.1","","expectation","Writing",{"withheld":1,"src":"https://dedigital.dde.pr/pluginfile.php/145102/mod_resource/content/6/Est%C3%A1ndares%20y%20Expectativas%20Programa%20de%20Ingl%C3%A9s.pdf"}],[0,"4.W.5.1a","","indicator","Writing",{"withheld":1,"src":"https://dedigital.dde.pr/pluginfile.php/145102/mod_resource/content/6/Est%C3%A1ndares%20y%20Expectativas%20Programa%20de%20Ingl%C3%A9s.pdf"}],[0,"4.W.5.1b","","indicator","Writing",{"withheld":1,"src":"https://dedigital.dde.pr/pluginfile.php/145102/mod_resource/content/6/Est%C3%A1ndares%20y%20Expectativas%20Programa%20de%20Ingl%C3%A9s.pdf"}],[0,"4.W.6","","standard","Writing",{"withheld":1,"src":"https://dedigital.dde.pr/pluginfile.php/145102/mod_resource/content/6/Est%C3%A1ndares%20y%20Expectativas%20Programa%20de%20Ingl%C3%A9s.pdf"}],[0,"4.W.6.1","","expectation","Writing",{"withheld":1,"src":"https://dedigital.dde.pr/pluginfile.php/145102/mod_resource/content/6/Est%C3%A1ndares%20y%20Expectativas%20Programa%20de%20Ingl%C3%A9s.pdf"}],[0,"4.W.7","","standard","Writing",{"withheld":1,"src":"https://dedigital.dde.pr/pluginfile.php/145102/mod_resource/content/6/Est%C3%A1ndares%20y%20Expectativas%20Programa%20de%20Ingl%C3%A9s.pdf"}],[0,"4.W.7.1","","expectation","Writing",{"withheld":1,"src":"https://dedigital.dde.pr/pluginfile.php/145102/mod_resource/content/6/Est%C3%A1ndares%20y%20Expectativas%20Programa%20de%20Ingl%C3%A9s.pdf"}],[0,"4.W.8","","standard","Writing",{"withheld":1,"src":"https://dedigital.dde.pr/pluginfile.php/145102/mod_resource/content/6/Est%C3%A1ndares%20y%20Expectativas%20Programa%20de%20Ingl%C3%A9s.pdf"}],[0,"4.W.8.1","","expectation","Writing",{"withheld":1,"src":"https://dedigital.dde.pr/pluginfile.php/145102/mod_resource/content/6/Est%C3%A1ndares%20y%20Expectativas%20Programa%20de%20Ingl%C3%A9s.pdf"}],[1,"128.6(b)(1)(A)","listen actively, ask relevant questions to clarify information, and make pertinent comments;","expectation","1",null],[1,"128.6(b)(1)(B)","follow, restate, and give oral instructions that involve a series of related sequences of action;","expectation","1",null],[1,"128.6(b)(1)(C)","express an opinion supported by accurate information, employing eye contact, speaking rate, volume, enunciation, and the conventions of language to communicate ideas effectively; and","expectation","1",null],[1,"128.6(b)(1)(D)","work collaboratively with others to develop a plan of shared responsibilities.","expectation","1",null],[1,"128.6(b)(2)(A)","demonstrate and apply phonetic knowledge by: (i) decoding palabras agudas, graves, esdrújulas, and sobresdrújulas (words with the stress on the last, penultimate, and antepenultimate syllable and words with the stress on the syllable before the antepenultimate); (ii) using orthographic rules to segment and combine syllables, including diphthongs and formal and accented hiatus; (iii) decoding and differentiating the meaning of a word based on the diacritical accent; and (iv) decoding words with prefixes and suffixes;","expectation","2",null],[1,"128.6(b)(2)(B)","demonstrate and apply spelling knowledge by: (i) spelling palabras agudas and graves (words with the stress on the last and penultimate syllable) with an orthographic accent; (ii) spelling palabras esdrújulas (words with the stress on the antepenultimate syllable) that have an orthographic accent; (iii) spelling words with diphthongs and hiatus; and (iv) marking accents appropriately when conjugating verbs such as in simple and imperfect past, past participle, perfect, conditional, and future tenses; and","expectation","2",null],[1,"128.6(b)(2)(C)","write legibly in cursive to complete assignments.","expectation","2",null],[1,"128.6(b)(3)(A)","use print or digital resources to determine meaning, syllabication, and pronunciation;","expectation","3",null],[1,"128.6(b)(3)(B)","use context within and beyond a sentence to determine the relevant meaning of unfamiliar words or multiple-meaning words;","expectation","3",null],[1,"128.6(b)(3)(C)","identify the meaning of and use words with affixes such as mono-, sobre-, sub-, inter-, poli-, -able, -ante, -eza, -ancia, and -ura, and roots, including auto, bio, grafía, metro, fono, and tele;","expectation","3",null],[1,"128.6(b)(3)(D)","identify, use, and explain the meaning of idioms, homographs, and homophones such as abrasar/abrazar; and","expectation","3",null],[1,"128.6(b)(3)(E)","differentiate between and use homographs, homophones, and commonly confused terms such as porque/porqué/por qué/por que, sino/si no, and también/tan bien.","expectation","3",null],[1,"128.6(b)(4)","Developing and sustaining foundational language skills: listening, speaking, reading, writing, and thinking--fluency. The student reads grade-level text with fluency and comprehension. The student is expected to use appropriate fluency (rate, accuracy, and prosody) when reading grade-level text.","strand","4",null],[1,"128.6(b)(5)","Developing and sustaining foundational language skills: listening, speaking, reading, writing, and thinking--self-sustained reading. The student reads grade appropriate texts independently. The student is expected to self-select text and read independently for a sustained period of time.","strand","5",null],[1,"128.6(b)(6)(A)","establish purpose for reading assigned and self-selected texts;","expectation","6",null],[1,"128.6(b)(6)(B)","generate questions about text before, during, and after reading to deepen understanding and gain information;","expectation","6",null],[1,"128.6(b)(6)(C)","make and correct or confirm predictions using text features, characteristics of genre, and structures;","expectation","6",null],[1,"128.6(b)(6)(D)","create mental images to deepen understanding;","expectation","6",null],[1,"128.6(b)(6)(E)","make connections to personal experiences, ideas in other texts, and society;","expectation","6",null],[1,"128.6(b)(6)(F)","make inferences and use evidence to support understanding;","expectation","6",null],[1,"128.6(b)(6)(G)","evaluate details read to determine key ideas;","expectation","6",null],[1,"128.6(b)(6)(H)","synthesize information to create new understanding; and","expectation","6",null],[1,"128.6(b)(6)(I)","monitor comprehension and make adjustments such as re-reading, using background knowledge, asking questions, and annotating when understanding breaks down.","expectation","6",null],[1,"128.6(b)(7)(A)","describe personal connections to a variety of sources, including self-selected texts;","expectation","7",null],[1,"128.6(b)(7)(B)","write responses that demonstrate understanding of texts, including comparing and contrasting ideas across a variety of sources;","expectation","7",null],[1,"128.6(b)(7)(C)","use text evidence to support an appropriate response;","expectation","7",null],[1,"128.6(b)(7)(D)","retell, paraphrase, or summarize texts in ways that maintain meaning and logical order;","expectation","7",null],[1,"128.6(b)(7)(E)","interact with sources in meaningful ways such as notetaking, annotating, freewriting, or illustrating;","expectation","7",null],[1,"128.6(b)(7)(F)","respond using newly acquired vocabulary as appropriate; and","expectation","7",null],[1,"128.6(b)(7)(G)","discuss specific ideas in the text that are important to the meaning.","expectation","7",null],[1,"128.6(b)(8)(A)","infer basic themes supported by text evidence;","expectation","8",null],[1,"128.6(b)(8)(B)","explain the interactions of the characters and the changes they undergo;","expectation","8",null],[1,"128.6(b)(8)(C)","analyze plot elements, including the rising action, climax, falling action, and resolution; and","expectation","8",null],[1,"128.6(b)(8)(D)","explain the influence of the setting, including historical and cultural settings, on the plot.","expectation","8",null],[1,"128.6(b)(9)(A)","demonstrate knowledge of distinguishing characteristics of well-known children's literature such as folktales, fables, legends, myths, and tall tales;","expectation","9",null],[1,"128.6(b)(9)(B)","explain figurative language such as simile, metaphor, and personification that the poet uses to create images;","expectation","9",null],[1,"128.6(b)(9)(C)","explain structure in drama such as character tags, acts, scenes, and stage directions;","expectation","9",null],[1,"128.6(b)(9)(D)","recognize characteristics and structures of informational text, including: (i) the central idea with supporting evidence; (ii) features such as pronunciation guides and diagrams to support understanding; and (iii) organizational patterns such as compare and contrast;","expectation","9",null],[1,"128.6(b)(9)(E)","recognize characteristics and structures of argumentative text by: (i) identifying the claim; (ii) explaining how the author has used facts for an argument; and (iii) identifying the intended audience or reader; and","expectation","9",null],[1,"128.6(b)(9)(F)","recognize characteristics of multimodal and digital texts.","expectation","9",null],[1,"128.6(b)(10)(A)","explain the author's purpose and message within a text;","expectation","10",null],[1,"128.6(b)(10)(B)","explain how the use of text structure contributes to the author's purpose;","expectation","10",null],[1,"128.6(b)(10)(C)","analyze the author's use of print and graphic features to achieve specific purposes;","expectation","10",null],[1,"128.6(b)(10)(D)","describe how the author's use of imagery, literal and figurative language such as simile and metaphor, and sound devices such as alliteration and assonance achieves specific purposes;","expectation","10",null],[1,"128.6(b)(10)(E)","identify and understand the use of literary devices, including first- or third-person point of view;","expectation","10",null],[1,"128.6(b)(10)(F)","discuss how the author's use of language contributes to voice; and","expectation","10",null],[1,"128.6(b)(10)(G)","identify and explain the use of anecdote.","expectation","10",null],[1,"128.6(b)(11)(A)","plan a first draft by selecting a genre for a particular topic, purpose, and audience using a range of strategies such as brainstorming, freewriting, and mapping;","expectation","11",null],[1,"128.6(b)(11)(B)","develop drafts into a focused, structured, and coherent piece of writing by: (i) organizing with purposeful structure, including an introduction, transitions, and a conclusion; and (ii) developing an engaging idea with relevant details;","expectation","11",null],[1,"128.6(b)(11)(C)","revise drafts to improve sentence structure and word choice by adding, deleting, combining, and rearranging ideas for coherence and clarity;","expectation","11",null],[1,"128.6(b)(11)(D)","edit drafts using standard Spanish conventions, including: (i) complete simple and compound sentences with subject-verb agreement and avoidance of splices, run-ons, and fragments; (ii) verb tense such as simple past, present, and future and imperfect past, past participle, and conditional; (iii) singular, plural, common, and proper nouns, including gender-specific articles; (iv) adjectives, including their comparative and superlative forms; (v) adverbs that convey frequency and adverbs that convey degree; (vi) prepositions and prepositional phrases; (vii) pronouns, including personal, possessive, objective, reflexive, and prepositional; (viii) coordinating conjunctions to form compound subjects, predicates, and sentences; (ix) capitalization of historical events and documents, titles of books, stories, and essays; (x) punctuation marks, including commas in compound and complex sentences and em dash for dialogue; and (xi) correct spelling of words with grade-appropriate orthographic patterns and rules; and","expectation","11",null],[1,"128.6(b)(11)(E)","publish written work for appropriate audiences.","expectation","11",null],[1,"128.6(b)(12)(A)","compose literary texts such as personal narratives and poetry using genre characteristics and craft;","expectation","12",null],[1,"128.6(b)(12)(B)","compose informational texts, including brief compositions that convey information about a topic, using a clear central idea and genre characteristics and craft;","expectation","12",null],[1,"128.6(b)(12)(C)","compose argumentative texts, including opinion essays using genre characteristics and craft; and","expectation","12",null],[1,"128.6(b)(12)(D)","compose correspondence that requests information.","expectation","12",null],[1,"128.6(b)(13)(A)","generate and clarify questions on a topic for formal and informal inquiry;","expectation","13",null],[1,"128.6(b)(13)(B)","develop and follow a research plan with adult assistance;","expectation","13",null],[1,"128.6(b)(13)(C)","identify and gather relevant information from a variety of sources;","expectation","13",null],[1,"128.6(b)(13)(D)","identify primary and secondary sources;","expectation","13",null],[1,"128.6(b)(13)(E)","demonstrate understanding of information gathered;","expectation","13",null],[1,"128.6(b)(13)(F)","recognize the difference between paraphrasing and plagiarism when using source materials;","expectation","13",null],[1,"128.6(b)(13)(G)","develop a bibliography; and","expectation","13",null],[1,"128.6(b)(13)(H)","use an appropriate mode of delivery, whether written, oral, or multimodal, to present results.","expectation","13",null]]}